; coverage test for the `nonassoc` keyword: declaring an infix operator non-associative makes
; `a OP b OP c` a ParseError (ambiguous: could mean `(a OP b) OP c` or `a OP (b OP c)`) instead
; of silently left-associating, while still allowing explicit parenthesization either way.
infix "myop" 20 20
bool "myop" 0
var x, y, z
nonassoc "myop"

; still fine: explicit grouping resolves the ambiguity either way
parse (x myop y) myop z
parse x myop (y myop z)

expect "ParseError"
    x myop y myop z
;;; Proof checked.
